From 01e8efb09e930f7375c192a2030eb30933bb8e98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:57:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: delete an ES port's VLAN br-port entry when the VLAN
 has no VNI

zebra_evpn_vl_mbr_deref() deletes the br-port entry of the VLAN an ES
port leaves only if the VLAN has a VNI. A DF or ES-VTEP change writes
the entry for every VLAN of the port, with or without a VNI, and a VNI
can be unmapped before the port leaves the VLAN. Either way the entry
stays in the dataplane after the port has left the VLAN.

Delete the VLAN's entry whenever an ES port leaves it.

Signed-off-by: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
---
 zebra/zebra_evpn_mh.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mh.c b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mh.c
index 4d428823cc..e77912597e 100644
--- a/zebra/zebra_evpn_mh.c
+++ b/zebra/zebra_evpn_mh.c
@@ -1017,9 +1017,11 @@ void zebra_evpn_vl_mbr_deref(uint16_t vid, struct zebra_if *zif)
 
 	list_delete_node(acc_bd->mbr_zifs, node);
 
-	if (acc_bd->zevpn && zif->es_info.es) {
+	if (zif->es_info.es) {
+		/* the VLAN's br-port entry is also written when it has no VNI */
 		dplane_br_port_delete(zif->ifp, vid);
-		zebra_evpn_local_es_evi_del(zif->es_info.es, acc_bd->zevpn);
+		if (acc_bd->zevpn)
+			zebra_evpn_local_es_evi_del(zif->es_info.es, acc_bd->zevpn);
 	}
 
 	/* if there are no other references the access_bd can be freed */
-- 
